--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The licence above covers this repository's own files - the program around
the Java VM (waterbox/), the patches, the tests and the documents - except
java/, the front end and sound mixer that run inside the VM with
FreeJ2ME-Plus. Those are under the GNU General Public License version 3 or
(at your option) any later version, like FreeJ2ME-Plus; the licence's text
is in extern/freej2me-plus/LICENSE.

The core this repository builds is made of other people's work:

- FreeJ2ME-Plus (extern/freej2me-plus, a submodule) is David Richardson's
  FreeJ2ME as continued by the FreeJ2ME-Plus authors, under the GNU General
  Public License version 3 or later (extern/freej2me-plus/LICENSE). It
  carries ObjectWeb ASM (BSD-3-Clause, in the same file) and JLayer (GNU
  Lesser General Public License 2 or later, src/javazoom).
- OpenJDK 21 (extern/jdk21u, a submodule): its HotSpot VM, built as Zero,
  is under the GNU General Public License version 2 only; its class library
  is under the same licence with the Classpath Exception
  (extern/jdk21u/LICENSE, ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION, ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO). The
  libraries OpenJDK carries are listed in its legal/ files.
- libffi (extern/libffi, a submodule), under the MIT licence.
- The DejaVu fonts, under the Bitstream Vera licence with DejaVu's changes
  in the public domain (waterbox/fonts-license/DejaVu.txt).

The program around the VM only calls into Java, as the java launcher does;
nothing in Java calls back into it.

The package this repository builds carries every one of those licence texts
(waterbox/package-licenses.json says which). It contains no game of
anyone's.
